Name each geometrical object. For each one, say whether reversing the two letters names the same object.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\node[left] at (-0.6,0) {(a)};
\draw (0,0)--(3,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$K$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$L$};
\node[left] at (-0.6,-1.5) {(b)};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.5)--(4,-1.5);
\fill (0,-1.5) circle (2pt) node[below] {$K$};
\fill (3,-1.5) circle (2pt) node[below] {$L$};
\node[left] at (-0.6,-3) {(c)};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-0.4,-3)--(4,-3);
\fill (0,-3) circle (2pt) node[below] {$K$};
\fill (3,-3) circle (2pt) node[below] {$L$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For the marked angle:
(a) name the vertex and the two arms
(b) give four valid three-letter names
(c) explain why $\angle NLP$ is not a correct name.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\usetikzlibrary{angles,arrows.meta}
\coordinate (N) at (0,0);
\coordinate (L) at (1.1,0);
\coordinate (M) at (3,0);
\coordinate (P) at (1.8,2.7);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (N)--(3.5,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (N)--(2.1,3.15);
\fill (N) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$N$};
\fill (L) circle (2pt) node[below] {$L$};
\fill (M) circle (2pt) node[below] {$M$};
\fill (P) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$P$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = L--N--P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

State all the equality information shown by the marks.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\usetikzlibrary{angles}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (2,3);
\coordinate (S) at (2,0);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\draw (R)--(S);
\fill (P) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$P$};
\fill (Q) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$Q$};
\fill (R) circle (2pt) node[above] {$R$};
\fill (S) circle (2pt) node[below] {$S$};
\draw (1,-0.12)--(1,0.12);
\draw (3,-0.12)--(3,0.12);
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = P--R--S};
\pic[draw,angle radius=1cm] {angle = S--R--Q};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Points $D$, $E$ and $F$ lie in that order on the ray shown.
(a) Name the same ray as ray $DE$ using $D$ and $F$.
(b) Explain why intervals $DE$ and $DF$ are different.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(5,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (1.8,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (3.8,0) circle (2pt);
\path (0,0) node[below] {$D$};
\path (1.8,0) node[below] {$E$};
\path (3.8,0) node[below] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
